  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN OCHA Centre for Humanitarian Data Phase 3, 2023-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Centre for Humanitarian Data (CHD)&apos;s business plan 2023-2027 contributes to OCHA&apos;s ambition to be more data-driven, analytical and to ensure responsible technology and data management. Priorities include: -  evolving the Humanitarian Data Exchange platform to be more sophisticated in its data processing and to preference data quality over quantity. - Using data science capability to undertake analysis that activates preemptive approaches to humanitarian crises, while pushing for accountability in analytical processes. - Reinforce adoption of data responsibility across the sector with new approaches to understanding and adapting to risks. - Reinforce the confidence of humanitarians to use data through training material and active learning. CHD aims to ensure data is central to decision making in the humanitarian sector, trust is at the forefront of data sharing and use and partnership and cross-sector collaboration underlie a strong data ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
